{"name":"Tiger King","hex":"#dd9922","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tiger","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Panthera tigris, a large predatory mammal of the cat family, indigenous to Asia.","A male tiger; as opposed to a tigress."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A final shouted phrase, accompanied by a jump or outstretched arms, at the end of a cheer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiger"},{"term":"king","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male monarch; a man who heads a monarchy; in an absolute monarchy, the supreme ruler of his nation.","The monarch with the most power and authority in a monarchy, regardless of sex."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To crown king, to make (a person) king.","To rule over as king."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/king"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tiger King","blocks":[{"text":"Tiger King is an American true crime documentary television series about the life of former zookeeper and convicted felon Joe Exotic. The first season was released on Netflix on March 20, 2020. A second season, Tiger King 2, was announced in September 2021 and was released on November 17, 2021, while a third season, Tiger King: The Doc Antle Story, was announced on December 3, 2021, and released one week later on December 12. The series focuses on the small but deeply interconnected society of big cat conservationists such as Carole Baskin, owner of Big Cat Rescue, and collectors such as Exotic, whom Baskin accuses of abusing and exploiting wild animals."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/14/Tiger_King%2C_Murder%2C_Mayhem_and_Madness_publicity_image.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger_King","wikidata":"Q88306935"},{"title":"Tiger","blocks":[{"text":"The tiger is a large cat and a member of the genus Panthera native to Asia. It has a powerful, muscular body with a large head and paws, a long tail and orange fur that fades to white in parts, with black, mostly vertical stripes. It is traditionally classified into nine subspecies, though some recognise only two subspecies, the mainland Asian tiger and the Sunda Islands tiger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg/330px-Bengal_tiger_%28Panthera_tigris_tigris%29_female_3_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger","wikidata":"Q19939"},{"title":"King","blocks":[{"text":"King is a royal title given to a male monarch. A king is an absolute monarch if he holds unrestricted governmental power or exercises full sovereignty over a nation. In a modern context, the title may refer to the ruler of one of a number of modern monarchies. The title of king is used alongside other titles for monarchs: in the West, emperor, grand prince, prince, archduke, duke or grand duke, and in the Islamic world, malik, sultan, emir or hakim, among others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg/330px-Aachen_Domschatz_Bueste1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King","wikidata":"Q12097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Joe_Exotic_%28Santa_Rose_County_Jail%29.png/500px-Joe_Exotic_%28Santa_Rose_County_Jail%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Joe_Exotic_%28Santa_Rose_County_Jail%29.png/500px-Joe_Exotic_%28Santa_Rose_County_Jail%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Joe Exotic, the main subject depicted in Tiger King, achieved a large following online and inspired several Internet memes.[49] He has expressed regret for his past actions.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoe_Exotic_(Santa_Rose_County_Jail).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Carole_Baskin_September_2019.png/500px-Carole_Baskin_September_2019.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Carole_Baskin_September_2019.png/1280px-Carole_Baskin_September_2019.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Carole_Baskin_September_2019.png/500px-Carole_Baskin_September_2019.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"As a result of Tiger King, several Internet memes targeted Carole Baskin for her speculated involvement in the disappearance of Don Lewis, her second husband.[53]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarole_Baskin_September_2019.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Tiger_distribution.png/500px-Tiger_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Tiger_distribution.png/1280px-Tiger_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Tiger_distribution.png/500px-Tiger_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATiger_distribution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Adult_male_Royal_Bengal_tiger.jpg/500px-Adult_male_Royal_Bengal_tiger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Adult_male_Royal_Bengal_tiger.jpg/1280px-Adult_male_Royal_Bengal_tiger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u